{"author":{"id":"d28e897521accad965e5a3acfc75f906eaa0157f711e26b2841e79fd25d0ef35"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788526590,"nonce":"/rXha2FuNkg1K+kZ0MeJFp7u/4w=","title":"janus_mantissa_fixed() calls removed _carry_to_balanced(), crashing panel for all units","message":"When janus_notation.py was updated (commit c8d9764) to replace the old right-to-left carry approach with the LSB-to-MSB extraction algorithm, to_balanced_dozenal_integer_digits() was correctly rewritten but _carry_to_balanced() was left as a dangling call inside janus_mantissa_fixed(). That function was not updated to use the new algorithm.\n\nThe consequence: any invocation of panel_genmon.py that triggers janus_mantissa_fixed() (which build_tokens() does unconditionally when ephem is present, for Solit) raises NameError: name '_carry_to_balanced' is not defined. The exception handler in main() catches this and outputs '[annit unavailable]' for every unit, so the panel shows no data at all -- including the Annit, which is the originally reported symptom.\n\nFix: rewrite the inline digit-extraction loop in janus_mantissa_fixed() to call to_balanced_dozenal_integer_digits(int(scaled)) instead of the old manual loop + _carry_to_balanced(), consistent with what janus_integer() and to_balanced_dozenal_mantissa_digits() already do.","files":null}]}